{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>ויאר</b> — twice in the Masorah: ויאר את הלילה, אל ה׳ ויאר לנו. And this is 'and the cloud and the darkness were for the Egyptians' — that the pillar of cloud did not depart as on other nights, but went behind them to bring darkness upon the Egyptians, while for Israel there was light, as written: אל ה׳ ויאר לנו." "<b>זה אל זה</b> — two instances juxtaposed. The other: וקרא זא אל זה. And he said: the ק ק ק (that) the angels sought to say shirah — the Holy One, Blessed be He, said to them: the work of My hands is drowning in the sea and you say shirah? And this is 'and this did not come near that' — those about whom it is said וקרא זא אל זה."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "The Hebrew reads דסמיכי דין 'two that are juxtaposed'; the second occurrence cited is from Isaiah 6:3 (וקרא זה אל זה), source address not written by the author. The angelic cry קדוש קדוש קדוש is represented here as ק׳ ק׳ ק׳ and the phrase מעשי ידי׳ as מעשי ידי ' (with apparent abbreviation for HaShem); rendered as shown."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:57.959496984Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}